BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/bboxrg-pete-hayes-the-contradictions-31st-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Pete Hayes & The Contradictions
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T230000
UID:d61718639c6aa98d43736163d0911b71@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Pete Hayes & The Contradictions w/ Color Palette & Jem Wilde! 
 Pete Hayes is the third version of his name. Some say the third and final 
 form. As a founding member of The Crystal Casino Band\, he now steps into 
 his own light\, carrying the flame of the “2014 tumblr indie rock” fro
 m his zillennial coming of age into something now deeper\, darker\, and mo
 re cinematic. Rooted in Washington\, DC\, his solo work channels the deadp
 an swagger of Lou Reed with the introspection of The National paired with 
 the grandeur of Phil Spector’s wall of sound. Pete Hayes is both a conti
 nuation and a rebirth\, finishing what he started\, and starting it all ov
 er again. \\*\\*\\* Color Palette\, led by principal songwriter/vocalist J
 ay Nemeyer\, is an indie dream pop band from Washington\, DC. Color Palett
 e creates lush auditory landscapes that feature shimmering\, pop-sensible 
 vocal and guitar melodies\, and the band has shared the stage with world-r
 enowned acts such as Charli XCX. Color Palette’s music has garnered plac
 ements with NBC Universal\, ESPN\, MTV\, Vimeo\, Volvo\, Aeropostale\, and
  Monster Energy. In July 2020\, they received a Wammie Award (Washington A
 rea Music Award) for Best Pop Song ("Marrakech to Bombay"). Color Palette 
 released a new EP in November 2025 (Zombie EP)\, and will continue releasi
 ng new music throughout 2026. \\*\\*\\* Jem Wilde is a Washington\, D.C.
 –based singer-songwriter whose music blends indie folk and folk-rock wit
 h intimate\, emotionally candid songwriting. His songs pair tender\, vibra
 nt melodies with deeply personal lyrics that explore themes such as queer 
 identity\, healing\, trauma\, and catharsis. A multidisciplinary artist wi
 th a background in poetry and classical dance\, Wilde brings a lyrical\, e
 xpressive sensibility to his performances and storytelling. Often describe
 d as ethereal and warm\, his music has drawn comparisons to artists like L
 ucy Dacus\, Soccer Mommy\, and Phoebe Bridgers\, earning him a growing fol
 lowing within the D.C. and Baltimore indie music communities.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/bboxrg-pete-hayes-the-contradictions-31st-jul-so
 ngbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
