BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/7dglb6-abby-holiday-charli-adams-7th-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Abby Holiday & Charli Adams
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T230000
UID:c80c34385c531c47bcb1d906238bd96d@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Women That Rock Summer Tour w/ Abby Holliday & Charli Adams an
 d Eliza Harrison Smith Friday August 7th \\*\\*\\* Nashville based singer-
 songwriter\, Abby Holliday\, has been writing songs for as long as she can
  recall. The 25-year-old burgeoning young artist is best known for explori
 ng serious themes without taking herself too seriously. Bearing resemblanc
 e to the sonic qualities of female icons Phoebe Bridgers and Japanese Hous
 e\, Holliday’s songwriting is a unique intersection of sad vibes\, intro
 spective lyricism\, and modern pop-sensibility. Holliday attempts to exami
 ne her external world as a skeptic — not a cynic — and her internal wo
 rld with honesty — not cruelty. By way of the journal entries that she c
 alls her songs\, Holliday invites others to do the very same. \\*\\*\\* Ha
 iling from Alabama\, Charli Adams is a singer-songwriter who found her mus
 ical calling at a young age. Leaving high school to finish online in a cof
 fee shop\, Adams’ relocated to Nashville\, Tennessee at 17 years old. He
 r makeshift college music history course was sifting through the dollar CD
  bin at her local record store\, while immersing herself in the vibrant lo
 cal scene. Testing out songs and honing her craft\, she began recording he
 r debut EP “Good At Being Young”. Her first release garnered recogniti
 on from none other than Taylor Swift\, who handpicked Charli's self-penned
  track\, "Backseat\," to be featured on her personally curated Women's Day
  Playlist on Apple Music. This co-sign marked the beginning of Charli's ri
 se in the industry. Charli released her critically-acclaimed debut album\,
  "Bullseye\," which earned high praise from respected publications such as
  EARMILK\, DORK\, The Fader\, NPR\, Billboard\, and Line of Best Fit. Coll
 aborations with renowned artists like Ruston Kelly\, Novo Amor\, and Night
 ly further solidified her reputation as an artist to watch. With an overfl
 owing passion for songwriting\, she has also penned songs for artists like
  Chloe Moriondo\, Yot Club\, Peach Pit\, Valley & many more. Charli's musi
 cal journey might have started in her bedroom\, but on the stage is where 
 her music truly comes alive. With an unmatched ability to connect with her
  audience on a personal level\, she quickly made a name for herself in the
  Nashville scene and beyond. Whether performing with her band or solo\, Ch
 arli's undeniable stage presence revealed that the spotlight is her natura
 l habitat. With a voice that resonates and a sound that captivates\, Charl
 i is an artist poised for greatness\, enchanting hearts with her unique bl
 end of haunting vocals and cinematic storytelling. \\*\\*\\* Indie-pop art
 ist Eliza Harrison Smith is making a name for herself in the independent m
 usic scene. Born and raised outside of Washington\, DC\, Eliza was a shy\,
  yet imaginative kid with a love for writing stories. When she picked up t
 he guitar in her teenage years\, those stories transformed into lyrics and
  melodies. Her passion for songwriting led her to Nashville\, Tennessee in
  2019. Since relocating to Nashville\, Eliza has released several singles 
 and two EPs\, slowly but steadily building a community around her music an
 d amassing streams in the millions. She has built momentum with Spotify an
 d Apple Music editorial placements and AAA radio play\, as well as headlin
 e shows in New York\, Nashville\, and DC. With soft\, emotive vocals\, inf
 ectious pop melodies and lyrics that strike a perfect balance of vulnerabi
 lity and cleverness\, Eliza’s music feels both emotionally honest and in
 stantly memorable. Her most recent EP\, “Same Old Dream”\, released in
  April of 2026.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/7dglb6-abby-holiday-charli-adams-7th-aug-songbyr
 d-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
