BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/oe7gng-w-ani-burn-that-bridge-tour-9th-sep-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Wé Ani - Burn That Bridge Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T230000
UID:874baab1deeb5ccb93ceceadd265d29c@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Don’t be fooled by her tiny speaking voice\, because she tur
 ns into a power-house vocalist as soon as she touches the mic. Wé Ani (Wa
 y Ah-nee) is a remarkable singer and performer who captivated audiences ar
 ound the world with her extraordinary voice. Born with a gift for music\, 
 Wé Ani discovered her passion for singing at the tender age of 12. From t
 hat moment on\, her journey in the music industry began to unfold\, leadin
 g her to remarkable achievements and unforgettable experiences. Wé Ani's 
 talent caught the attention of many when she showcased her vocal prowess o
 n the hit TV show\, The Voice. Competing against an array of talented arti
 sts\, Wé Ani left an indelible mark and secured a remarkable 3rd place fi
 nish\, winning the hearts of viewers with her soulful and powerful perform
 ances. Prior to her appearance on The Voice\, Wé Ani honed her skills at 
 the prestigious Harlem School of the Arts\, refining her technique and dev
 eloping her unique style. Her dedication and hard work paid off when\, at 
 the age of 16\, she triumphed on four separate occasions at the renowned A
 pollo Theater in New York City\, solidifying her status as an exceptional 
 vocalist. Wé Ani's talent knows no bounds\, and her music has taken her a
 cross the United States and beyond. Sharing the stage with legendary artis
 ts such as Stevie Wonder\, Josh Groban\, Chris Botti\, Ceelo Green\, Patti
  Austin\, Dionne Warwick\, John Legend\, and Alicia Keys\, Wé Ani has pro
 ven herself to be a versatile and dynamic performer\, captivating audience
 s with her incredible vocal range and stage presence. Her talents have bee
 n recognized and celebrated on numerous prestigious platforms. Wé Ani had
  the honor of performing at the Gershwin Prize Tribute\, a tribute to the 
 legendary Tony Bennett\, held at the Library of Congress. She also showcas
 ed her skills in the rock and roll off-Broadway play Rocktopia\, where she
  shared the stage with renowned musician Dee Snider.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/oe7gng-w-ani-burn-that-bridge-tour-9th-sep-songb
 yrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
